.TH CRUNCH_MQ_UNLINK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_mq_unlink \- Linux x86-64 syscall 241
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int crunch_mq_unlink(const char* name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unlinks a queue using the raw kernel name, without a leading slash.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mq_unlink (2)
